    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm putting together a hypertrophy plan for a client. can you explain the specific role leucine plays in triggering the mTOR pathway? also need to know how a caloric surplus impacts nitrogen balance for optimal protein synthesis. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a primary activator of the mTORC1 pathway by binding to the RAK7 complex on the ribosome, which directly initiates the signaling cascade required for muscle protein synthesis. Regarding your second point, maintaining a caloric surplus creates a positive nitrogen balance as the body prioritizes storing amino acids as new muscle tissue rather than offsetting them with energy expenditure. This combination of sufficient leucine thresholds and positive energy balance maximizes the anabolic response for hypertrophy.",
